## 🔄 Part C — The Operating Cadence

Governance is a rhythm, not an event. Each ritual has an owner, inputs, and outputs that feed the next.

### Weekly — Triage (AI Gov Lead, 30 min)
- **In:** new intake forms (Day 35), incidents (Day 37), monitoring alerts
- **Do:** tier new use cases, assign owners, route Tier 1s to the board queue
- **Out:** updated intake pipeline; escalations flagged

### Monthly — Governance Board (Chair, 60–90 min)
- **In:** Tier 1 approvals, Critical/High risks (Day 34), model-card sign-offs (Day 36), incident post-mortems (Day 37), KPI dashboard
- **Do:** decide go-lives, accept/reject residual risks, review incidents, unblock
- **Out:** recorded decisions; corrective actions with owners/dates

### Quarterly — Program Review (Chair → Exec Committee, 60 min)
- **In:** KPI trends, maturity assessment, regulatory horizon scan, audit findings
- **Do:** report program health to executives; adjust policy, budget, priorities
- **Out:** exec-level report; policy updates; resourcing decisions

### Annually — Independent Review
- External or internal-audit review against ISO 42001; refresh risk taxonomy and policy; re-baseline the maturity model.

