## 📊 Part D — The KPI Dashboard

Twelve metrics across four lenses. This is what makes the program *measurable* — and what a VP shows the board to prove ROI and control.

### Coverage — *do we know what AI we have?*
| KPI | Target |
|-----|--------|
| % of known AI systems with a completed AIA | ≥ 95% |
| % of production systems with a current model card | ≥ 90% |
| Shadow-AI systems discovered → registered this quarter | Trending down |

### Risk — *how much exposure are we carrying?*
| KPI | Target |
|-----|--------|
| # of open Critical / High risks | Critical = 0 |
| Avg. residual risk score across the portfolio | Trending down |
| % of Critical/High risks past their treatment SLA | 0% |

### Speed — *is governance enabling or blocking?*
| KPI | Target |
|-----|--------|
| Median time from intake → decision (Tier 2) | ≤ 5 business days |
| Median time from intake → decision (Tier 1) | ≤ 1 board cycle |
| % of use cases cleared at triage without full review | ≥ 70% |

### Outcomes — *is it actually working?*
| KPI | Target |
|-----|--------|
| # of AI incidents by severity (trend) | SEV-1 = 0 |
| Mean time to contain (MTTC) an AI incident | ≤ 4 hours (SEV-1/2) |
| % of incidents that fed a register/model-card update | 100% |

> **The two numbers execs care about most:** *"How fast can we ship AI safely?"* (Speed) and *"What's our worst unmitigated exposure?"* (open Criticals). Lead with those.

